     6	
     7	## EP1 — canonical client address has one trust boundary
     8	
     9	Direct requests use the socket peer address. Forwarded address headers are ignored unless the
    10	immediate peer exactly matches an explicitly configured trusted-proxy allowlist. Trusted requests
    11	accept one bounded, strictly parsed forwarding chain and select the configured hop; malformed,
    12	overlong, ambiguous, or mixed forwarding headers fail typed before authentication/provider/body
    13	work. Audit records retain only a presence/classification and a keyed address digest, never the raw
    14	address. Empty proxy trust means direct mode.
    15	All accepted addresses are canonicalized before exact allowlist membership, quota keys, or digests.
    16	Equivalent IPv6 spellings share one identity, and IPv4-mapped IPv6 is explicitly canonicalized to
    17	IPv4; normalization never grants subnet, implicit loopback, or non-exact trust.
    18	Quoted `Forwarded` values are accepted only through a deliberately small escape-free grammar;
    19	protocol tokens are case-insensitive HTTP/HTTPS after decoding, while controls, escapes, duplicate
    20	or unknown parameters, zones, ports, and ambiguous forms remain refused.
    21	
    22	## EP2 — deterministic bounded quota authority
    23	
    24	A dependency-free quota authority enforces fixed-window limits with an injected clock, bounded key
    25	cardinality, deterministic expiry, and no randomness. Separate policies cover unauthenticated login
    26	attempts per canonical address, all HTTP requests per address, authenticated commands per
    27	credential, weighted command cost, stream-ticket issuance, and concurrent connections. Limit
    28	configuration rejects zero, negative, non-integer, unbounded, or internally inconsistent values.
    29	Every clock sample must be a non-negative safe integer and monotonic for its quota; an invalid or
    30	regressing sample fails before expiry, key, or counter mutation and can never produce refusal
    31	metadata. `Retry-After` is always a positive finite integer bounded by the configured window.
    32	Ticket quota uses an in-process reservation that commits only when issuance succeeds and rolls back
    33	on capacity, clock/randomness, audit, or other issuance failure.
    34	
    35	## EP3 — refusal precedes expensive or privileged work
    36	
    37	The address quota runs before body parsing, identity-provider execution, session mutation, or
    38	coordinator dispatch. Login throttling therefore bounds provider calls. Principal/cost quota runs
    39	after authentication but before durable command admission or dispatch. Refusal returns bounded
    40	`429 rate_limited` plus `Retry-After`, is audited fail closed, and mutates no session, command,
    41	worker, or stream state. The login-attempt quota applies only to the admitted `POST` login route;
    42	canonical HTTPS, exact Origin, JSON content type, bounded valid JSON, and an object body are all
    43	validated before it is consumed. Preflight, invalid methods, and other policy-invalid requests use
    44	the ordinary address quota but cannot consume login attempts. Stream-ticket Origin, repository,
    45	capability, and live-principal authorization likewise precede the credential ticket quota.
    46	Client-supplied IDs cannot choose a quota bucket.
    47	Request targets are bounded origin-form strings with valid percent encoding; malformed, overlong,
    48	non-string, control-bearing, absolute, scheme-relative, or fragment-bearing targets fail as one
    49	typed audited refusal before authentication, provider, session, or fleet work.
